<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:ext="http://exslt.org/common"><head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
<title>IRS_SPI_VMR | Jon's Arm Reference</title><meta name="description" content="IRS SPI VM Assignment Register."></meta><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"></meta><link rel="stylesheet" href="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.css"></link><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/static/normalize.css"></link><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/static/main.css"></link></head><body><p class="discontinuation-notice" data-pagefind-ignore="all"><b>PER ARM'S REQUEST, THIS SITE WILL BE DISCONTINUED ON 4 DECEMBER 2026. :(</b><br></br>

      Arm's lawyers have notified me to take down this site or face legal action. <br></br>

      To all of the fans of this site over the years (even the ones at Arm): thank you for your support! I'm glad I could provide a resource so many people found value in. I will look into solutions that can potentially keep bookmarks and links working. <br></br>

      — Jon
    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">IRS_SPI_VMR</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">IRS SPI VM Assignment Register</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>IRS SPI VM Assignment Register.</p>

      
        <p>Allows software to read and update the VM assignment of the SPI selected by <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_selr.html">IRS_SPI_SELR</a>.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>This register is present only when FEAT_GICv5_EXT is implemented and IRS_IDR0.VIRT == '1'. Otherwise, direct accesses to IRS_SPI_VMR are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
        <p>The effects of a write to this register are not guaranteed to have completed before <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_statusr.html">IRS_SPI_STATUSR</a>.IDLE is 1.</p>

      
        <p>Following a write to this register, <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_statusr.html">IRS_SPI_STATUSR</a>.V is updated.</p>
      <h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>IRS_SPI_VMR is a 64-bit register.</p>
      <p>This  register is part of the <a href="irs_config_frame.html">IRS_CONFIG_FRAME</a> block.</p><h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>63</td><td>62</td><td>61</td><td>60</td><td>59</td><td>58</td><td>57</td><td>56</td><td>55</td><td>54</td><td>53</td><td>52</td><td>51</td><td>50</td><td>49</td><td>48</td><td>47</td><td>46</td><td>45</td><td>44</td><td>43</td><td>42</td><td>41</td><td>40</td><td>39</td><td>38</td><td>37</td><td>36</td><td>35</td><td>34</td><td>33</td><td>32</td></tr></thead><tfoot><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></tfoot><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="1"><a href="#fieldset_0-63_63">VIRT</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="31"><a href="#fieldset_0-62_16">RES0</a></td></tr><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-62_16">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-15_0">VM_ID</a></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="text_before_fields">
    <p>This register is updated after a write to <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_selr.html">IRS_SPI_SELR</a> when <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_statusr.html">IRS_SPI_STATUSR</a>.{V, IDLE} is {1, 1}.</p>
  </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-63_63">VIRT, bit [63]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Whether the SPI selected by <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_selr.html">IRS_SPI_SELR</a> is assigned as a virtual SPI to the VM.</p>
    <table class="valuetable"><tr><th>VIRT</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b0</td><td>
          <p>The SPI is not assigned to a VM.</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b1</td><td>
          <p>The SPI is assigned to the VM specified by VM_ID.</p>
        </td></tr></table></div><h4 id="fieldset_0-62_16">Bits [62:16]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-15_0">VM_ID, bits [15:0]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Identifies the VM that the SPI selected by <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_selr.html">IRS_SPI_SELR</a> is assigned to.</p>
    
      <p>Following a write to <a href="irs_config_frame.irs_spi_selr.html">IRS_SPI_SELR</a>, when IRS_SPI_VMR.VIRT is 0, this field is set to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</p>
    <p>Accessing this field has the following behavior:</p><ul><li>When IRS_SPI_VMR.VIRT == '1', access to this field
                            is <span class="access_level">RO</span>.
                        </li><li>
                  Otherwise,
                  
                  access to this field
                  is <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
                </li></ul></div><div class="access_mechanisms"><h2>Access Instructions</h2>
        <p>When the value of VIRT in the register is 1, meaning that the selected SPI is assigned to a VM, any write that does not set VIRT to 0 is ignored.</p>

      
        <p>To assign an SPI to a different VM, the SPI must first be unassigned from the old VM, and then subsequently assigned to the new VM.</p>
      <p>Accesses to this register use the following encodings:</p><div class="access_block"><p>Accessible at offset <span class="hexnumber">0x0100</span> from IRS_CONFIG_FRAME</p></div><ul><li>When IRS_SPI_STATUSR.[V,IDLE] != '11', accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">UNKNOWN/WI</span>.
          </li><li>When !IsSPIDVISupported(IRS_SPI_SELR.ID), accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RAZ/WI</span>.
          </li><li>Otherwise, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
          </li></ul><p style="text-align: right">
      ()
      </p></div><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
